maybe you feel that European  institutions are far removed from your  everyday life well in fact the European  Parliament is much closer to home than  you could ever have imagined it's  present in all Member States through its  information offices even in Washington  DC these information officers are the  go-to places for answers in your own  language on the role and activities of  the European Parliament and its members  as well as all EU policies they also  provide free information material  organised debates with MEP s and stake  holders and keep the media informed as  news from the Parliament through press  briefings information officers work  closely with teachers and schools to  make the European Parliament accessible  and comprehensible to young people  through seminars and debates designed  especially for them they also organize a  competition called Euro Scholar that  gives students from all Member States if  selected the chance to become an MEP for  a day at the Parliament seat in  Strasbourg in France to keep their  finger on the pulse of citizens need for  up-to-date news and information  information officers are in touch with  many different professional groups local  authorities companies non-government  organizations and anyone else who has an  interest in European affairs and the  role of the European Parliament so where  is your nearest information point to  find it all you have to do is to type  European Parliament information office  in your browser and it'll all appear  before your very eyes oh and one more  thing we'll forget to follow them on  social media too
 

